.TH "ZEPHYR" "1" "September 2026" "zephyr" "zephyr Manual"
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBzephyr\fR \- Nim policy and workflow controller
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBzephyr\fR \fIdomain\fR \fIaction\fR [\fIargs\fR\.\.\.]
.
.P
Commands may be chained with \fB\.\fR\.
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBzephyr\fR is the policy, workflow, geometry, and filesystem helper layer for Cirrus\. It provides higher\-level window, group, layout, rule, and state operations while preserving explicit window IDs for action targeting\.
.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.
.SS "DISPLAY"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay height\fR: Print display height\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay width\fR: Print display width\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay width_test\fR \fIargs\fR: Test the configured display width\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.SS "SCREEN"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen gap\fR: Print the configured gap\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen indent\fR: Print the configured indentation\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen margin\fR: Print the configured margin\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen panel\fR: Print panel height/position information\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen top\fR: Print the configured top offset\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen bottom\fR: Print the configured bottom offset\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.SS "GROUP"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup add\fR \fIgroup\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Add a window to a public group\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup remove\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Remove a window from its group\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup close\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Close the selected group/window workflow target\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup count\fR: Print the configured group count\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup current\fR: Print the selected filesystem/current group\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup desktop\fR \fIargs\fR: Run the desktop compatibility workflow\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup focus\fR \fIargs\fR: Navigate to a group\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup id\fR \fIname\fR: Print a group\'s public numeric ID\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup last\fR: Run the previous\-group workflow\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup name\fR [\fIgroup\fR]: Print a group name\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup reconcile\fR \fIgroup\fR: Reconcile the filesystem current\-group mirror\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup restore\fR: Restore the saved group state\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup toggle\fR \fIargs\fR: Toggle group visibility/selection\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
Public group IDs are one\-based\. \fB0\fR is not a public group argument\.
.
.SS "WINDOW"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow await\fR \fIselector\fR [\fIproperty\fR]: Wait for a matching window/property\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow classname\fR: Print the focused window class\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow count\fR [\fIselector\fR]: Count matching windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow extend\fR \fIargs\fR: Extend the selected window toward a direction/side\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow geometry\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Print geometry for an explicit or focused window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow group\fR \fIgroup\fR [\-\-teleport]: Assign the focused window to a public group; \fB\-\-teleport\fR additionally applies the existing teleport workflow\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow layer\fR \fInormal|above|overlay\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Set a persistent WM stacking layer without changing focus\. \fBoverlay\fR stays above \fBabove\fR, which stays above \fBnormal\fR\. The target defaults to the focused window; normal restores ordinary stacking\. An explicit assignment overrides EWMH defaults until the managed client is destroyed/unmanaged, including across hide/remap\. Title\-case layer names remain accepted\. Docks and EWMH ABOVE windows automatically participate in the WM above tier without zephyr or zephyrd rules\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow hide\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Hide a window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow ids\fR [\-\-all] [\fIclassname\fR] [\-\-name \fIname\fR] [\-\-group \fIgroup\fR]: Print matching window IDs through the daemon cache\. \fB\-\-group\fR narrows the existing visibility and class/name filters without implying \fB\-\-all\fR\. Group IDs match \fBsirocco group add\fR directly; zero is invalid\. Membership is refreshed by the existing WM snapshot/invalidation path, including after daemon restart\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow restore\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Restore saved window geometry\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow rotate\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Swap the selected window\'s width and height\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow shift\fR \fIargs\fR: Shift the selected window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow size\fR \fIargs\fR: Set or adjust the selected window\'s size\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
`window move \fIargs\fR: Move the selected window by X Y pixels\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow snap\fR \fIargs\fR: Snap the selected window to a screen position\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow spread\fR \fIargs\fR: Spread the selected window across a region\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow stack\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Print the overlap\-connected stack for a window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow swap\fR \fIargs\fR: Swap window geometry/state as requested\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow tile\fR \fIargs\fR: Tile the selected window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow toggle\fR \fIargs\fR: Toggle matching windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow wm\-group\fR \fIwinid\fR: Print the WM\-reported group for an explicit ID\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow wm\-groups\fR: Print WM groups for managed windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow snapshot\fR: Print the normalized WM snapshot\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
\fBwm\-group\fR, \fBwm\-groups\fR, and \fBsnapshot\fR are read\-only observations\. The \fBwindow stack\-geometries\fR and \fBwindow apply\-geometries\fR commands are Sirocco commands; they are not zephyr public actions\.
.
.SS "LAYOUT"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout explode\fR: Capture the current overlap\-connected stack, save original geometry, and arrange those windows according to the existing layout rule\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout unexplode\fR: Restore saved geometry for surviving exploded windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout explode \-\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR: Place visible group members using the fold grid engine and save a dedicated identity\-bearing explode operation under \fB$WME/layout/explode:group:N\fR\. Each group retains independent state\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout unexplode \-\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR: Restore that recorded operation, including surviving clients that changed groups or became hidden\. New members and reused XIDs with different identity tokens are not restored\. Preserve current focus and remove the saved operation after restoration\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout fold\fR \fIargs\fR: Fold matching windows into a grid, then raise participants in placement order within their effective stacking bands while preserving focus\. Repeating an unchanged fold still raises the selected set\. Group explode shares this stacking behavior without sharing fold transaction ownership\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout level\fR \fIargs\fR: Level windows vertically\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout restore\fR [\fIargs\fR]: Restore layout state\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout spread\fR \fIargs\fR: Spread windows across a grid\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout tile\fR \fIargs\fR: Tile windows into a grid\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
\fBunexplode\fR ignores disappeared saved XIDs and preserves the current focus\.
.
.SS "RULE"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBrule\fR \fIname\fR: Apply a configured application rule\. Rule names are the names implemented by the current rule dispatcher\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.SS "STATE"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBstate snapshot\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Save a window geometry snapshot\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBstate restore\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Restore a saved window geometry snapshot\.
.
.IP "" 0
.
.P
\fBzephyrd\fR removes \fB$WINFO/<winid>\fR after receiving an actual X11 \fBDestroyNotify\fR and confirming that the window no longer exists\. Hidden, unmapped, and inactive\-group windows retain their state\. Startup and X11 reconnection also reconcile stale WINFO directories, including windows that died while the daemon was stopped\. Uncertain X11 errors preserve state\.
.
.P
The same lifecycle handler reconciles \fB$HIDDEN/<winid>\fR on \fBMapNotify\fR and \fBDestroyNotify\fR, checking current X visibility before removing an entry\. Visible or destroyed windows lose hidden metadata; genuinely unmapped windows retain it\. Startup/reconnection scans both trees, including hidden entries without WINFO records\. No particular focus or restore command is required\.
.
.P
WINFO cleanup waits for active restore\-history transactions and retries deferred work; HIDDEN cleanup proceeds independently\. Group membership and focus records remain owned by WM snapshot reconciliation\. Correctness does not require an explicit \fBzephyr group close\fR before closing an application\.
.
.SH "CHAINING"
Commands can be sequenced with a period:
.
.IP "" 4
.
.nf

zephyr window move 10 10 0x01234567 \. window size 800x600 0x01234567
.
.fi
.
.IP "" 0
.
